    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Kaltura is showing early signs of operational momentum, with demand trends allowing the company to exceed its own revenue and profitability guidance in what is typically a seasonally soft quarter. The positive operating cash flow milestone, achieved for the first time in a first quarter, signals improving business fundamentals. Simultaneously, the company is evolving its product narrative toward an AI-powered platform, suggesting an effort to capture a new wave of enterprise video and content personalization demand. The competitive backdrop is not detailed, but the M&A activity indicates an active attempt to reposition and widen its offering.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership delivered a credible beat-and-raise posture, translating top-line strength into stronger adjusted profitability and generating cash from operations. The recent PathFactory acquisition underscores a deliberate strategy to accelerate the build-out of an AI-centric platform, moving beyond organic development alone. Closing the deal and immediately framing it around the AI story suggests management is acting with intent to reshape its growth narrative. While the underlying business still shows accounting losses, the sequential improvement in cash generation and guidance execution is likely to begin repairing market credibility.",
